Phase 2 panel bring-up (2026-09-19, docs/kernel-boot-debugging.md
Rounds 38-46, docs/phase2-panel-scoping.md): a new
"samsung,gts7l-ppa957db1-nt36523" entry in mainline's existing
drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36523.c (not a new driver from
scratch - this file already supports the same NT36523 chip family on
Xiaomi's elish, a directly comparable SM8250 tablet); a small new
drivers/misc/isl98608-gts7l.c for this device's separate LCD bias IC
(single fixed register program at probe, matching the downstream
driver's own behavior exactly); a board-specific PHY analog trim
override added to drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c (mirroring
dsi_phy_10nm.c's own existing parse_dt_properties/tuning_cfg precedent),
since mainline's generic hardcoded trim constants for this SoC
generation's C-PHY path don't match Samsung's own downstream
calibration for this exact panel/PHY pairing (confirmed working on real
hardware - the real PLL locks 5x during the actual modeset with this
fix, no failures); MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO_BURST on gts7l_desc's mode_flags,
matching downstream's own qcom,mdss-dsi-traffic-mode = "burst_mode" for
this exact panel; and (Round 46) has_dcs_backlight = false, since the
automatic backlight_device registration this flag enables triggers an
unsynchronized dsi->mode_flags read-modify-write that races the DRM
commit path and corrupts MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO - a documented mainline
bug class, confirmed on real hardware to be the direct, repeatable
cause of "dsi_err_worker: status=4" (DSI_ERR_STATE_FIFO). Also
registers this project's own DTB in arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/Makefile
(should have been saved earlier, alongside 0001/0002 - the DTS itself
lives at kernel/dts/sm8250-samsung-gts7l.dts in this repo, synced into
a working kernel tree before building; this patch covers everything
else that had to change in the wider kernel source tree).

Also includes temporary diagnostic pr_err()s (all tagged "gts7l
temporary diagnostic" inline) in drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
(raw REG_DSI_FIFO_STATUS value) and dsi_phy_7nm.c (confirming
dsi_7nm_phy_enable/dsi_pll_7nm_vco_prepare are reached and what trim
values land) and isl98608-gts7l.c (probe success) - left in as of this
patch since they're part of what's actually been tested on real
hardware; safe to strip once display bring-up is fully confirmed
working, not required for correctness.

Applies on top of Linux 7.2 (work/linux's checked-out commit
8d3ae59288f1e7d58d76558a6ee96d533bc5019f) with 0001/0002 already
applied.

